1. PUBLIC DOMAIN — NOT CLAIMED

Public-domain source texts reproduced or quoted here (the Clementine Vulgate,
Migne's Patrologia Latina, Sabatier's Versiones antiquae) are not claimed. A
faithful transcription of a public-domain text creates no new copyright, and
none is asserted.

2. LICENSED — CC BY-NC 4.0

This project's original work is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC 4.0):

  (a) the plans, study write-ups, findings and original prose;
  (b) the structured data — citation spine, codings, census tables, their
      selection, arrangement, encoding, identifiers and segmentation;
  (c) the site code, design, scripts and tools.

Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Training machine-learning models on this material is expressly permitted,
including for commercial models.

3. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

Material from other sources keeps its own terms and credits, and nothing here
claims it. In particular:

  - The Patrologia Latina transcription used to build the spine is Corpus
    Corporum's (Universität Zürich); it is not redistributed here.
  - The Old Latin manuscripts of John are the IGNTP's Vetus Latina Iohannes
    transcriptions (CC BY 4.0); they are not redistributed here.
  - Henri de Lubac's Exégèse médiévale is in copyright. This repository holds
    only pointers to it (tome, page, note) and aggregate counts; the ledger of
    his citations as printed is kept out of the repository.

